$ secskills token verify --file <SANDBOX>/signed.json
signature OK — tenant acme, AS64500, 1 prefixes, window <TIME>..<TIME>, classes [cve tls], intrusive=false
[exit 0]

$ secskills token verify --file <SANDBOX>/signed.json --ip 203.0.113.17 --class cve
signature OK — tenant acme, AS64500, 1 prefixes, window <TIME>..<TIME>, classes [cve tls], intrusive=false
authorizes 203.0.113.17 (cve): true — authorized by token for acme
[exit 0]

$ secskills token verify --file <SANDBOX>/signed.json --ip 198.51.100.1 --class cve
signature OK — tenant acme, AS64500, 1 prefixes, window <TIME>..<TIME>, classes [cve tls], intrusive=false
authorizes 198.51.100.1 (cve): false — target outside the token's prefixes
[exit 0]

$ secskills token verify --file <SANDBOX>/signed.json --ip 203.0.113.17 --class exploit
signature OK — tenant acme, AS64500, 1 prefixes, window <TIME>..<TIME>, classes [cve tls], intrusive=false
authorizes 203.0.113.17 (exploit): false — check class exploit not in allowed_classes
